<title>USA: Amoco expected to issue $200 mln 10-yr debt.</title>
<headline>Amoco expected to issue $200 mln 10-yr debt.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-08-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Amoco Corp, a major integrated oil firm, is expected to tap the corporate bond market with a $200 million debt offering, dealers said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The deal, which is expected to include a 10-year maturity, will be underwritten by Morgan Stanley Dean Witter, dealers said.</p>
<p>Goldman Sachs &amp; Co and Credit Suisse First Boston are among the other underwriters on the deal, they said.</p>
<p>No further details were available.</p>
<p>((--Nancy Leinfuss, U.S. Corporate Bond Unit, 212-859-1675 ))</p>
